  "body": "@isaacs mentioned this previously, both in his `poll` + `state` + `readCurrentBufferSynchronously` API, and in discussion of how writable streams should work.\n\nFor writable streams, `write()` will return a promise, but there still needs to be a backpressure signal; Node.js has that be the return value, since it uses callbacks for asynchrony. But a property of the writable stream is probably the way to go.\n",
